# CI/CD and Quality Gates

Automated checks and release-readiness gates for the frontend.

## Requirements

- CI must fail on formatting differences, analyzer errors, or failing required tests.
- CI must fail when committed generated code is stale.
- CI must not use production credentials and must not print secrets.
- Release builds must use production-safe configuration.
- Deployment scripts must be POSIX-friendly for Linux/macOS hosts; platform builds may split by OS when tooling requires.

## Local quality commands

```bash
flutter pub get
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
dart format --set-exit-if-changed .
flutter analyze
flutter test
```

Run generation before analysis only when the project uses generated files.

## Release checklist

- Version, formatting, analyzer, and tests pass.
- Generated code is current when generation is used.
- No secrets committed; production API URL and logging level correct.
- Supported platform builds complete on compatible hosts.

## Acceptance

- CI reproduces the local quality-gate commands.
- Builds are deterministic enough for release packaging.
- Platform host requirements are documented.

